    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214-a3">

                <pb facs="0512" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg416"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in Mr. Hathorne’s No.
                    42.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kirk to Mr. Hathorne.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Zanzibar</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 27,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your letter of 26th instant was delivered
                    to me this morning. I at once forwarded a copy to Captain Earle, of Her
                    Majesty’s ship London.</p>
                <p>I am now informed that the negroes referred to by you have been sent back to the
                    American bark Laconia, and that a full report of the circumstances of the case
                    will be prepared for your information.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN KIRK,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Her Majesty’s Agent and
                            Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
